MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=14
DESCRIPTION=Relay chat, announcements and cat show text as sent instead of '?'. Untrusted text in the freestanding image (relay messages, host announcements, cat/type of a received file) is printed one unit at a time: printable ASCII as is, a tab as one space, valid UTF-8 as its code page 437 glyph on the VGA screen (the original bytes on serial and in redirects; '?' only for a character the VGA font has no glyph for), other control bytes as caret text (ESC [ 2 J shows as ^[[2J, BEL as ^G, DEL as ^?), and a byte that is not valid UTF-8 as \xNN. A line break inside a relayed message or announcement becomes a new line indented two spaces (a trailing one adds nothing), so it still cannot start a forged lab control line; cat keeps its [file] prefix per line. When a sender's colour code sets the foreground back to the default (0, 39 or an empty SGR), the recipient's role colour comes back, so the rest of a chat message stays cyan. Host announcements: `server announce` now sends the relay's SERVER_ANNOUNCE frame (server-relay-client.js sendAnnouncement, host only; session-relay-room.js relays it from the host to every other member and answers anyone else with "server announce: host only"; the BroadcastChannel fallback carries it too), and the page types it into each other guest as `relayannounce [+] <hex>` in the same 48-byte parts as chat (lab-core.js relayAnnounceLines). The guest prints it in bright blue (SGR 94; VGA blue is hard to read on black) as `[Server Announcement]: <text>`, wrapped at 80 columns with the same text rules, matching the hosted fl_color_announce; relayannounce needs an armed server seat and is kept off the VGA screen like relayrecv. The lab page's canvas draws code page 437 glyphs for screen bytes 128-255 (lab-core.js cp437Char). Tests: test-freestanding-shell (line breaks, caret text, \xNN, UTF-8 on serial and code page 437 on VGA, cyan after a reset, blue announcement, announcement parts never joining chat, cat), test_browser_lab (relayAnnounceLines, cp437Char, indented lines inert) and test_lab_relay_room (host-only announce).
